# The Crooked Moon's gaze (plan 5.5, story/ritual_track.gd): what the Narrator says as a fight starts under the moon, one line
# for each stage of the ritual track, each once a playthrough, only under the open sky. The Vagrant tells it afterwards:
# second person, present tense, one or two sentences, no game words (the engine's docs/design/narration.md).
# First draft by Claude; Gemini edits it with the next Narrator batch.

~ combat:moon
| [once and attention >= grinning and attention < wide and not indoors] The moon leans down to watch, and you could swear it's smiling wider than it was.
| [once and attention >= wide and attention < leering and not indoors] The moon's light goes green at the edges as the steel comes out, like it's been waiting all night for this.
| [once and attention >= leering and attention < full and not indoors] Up above, that crooked grin has opened clear to the back teeth, and it doesn't blink.
| [once and attention >= full and not indoors] The whole sky is one red grin now, and every shadow on this ground points the same way: at you.
